<title>SOUTH KOREA: Hanbo dropped from KOSPI-200 index pool.</title>
<headline>Hanbo dropped from KOSPI-200 index pool.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Korea Stock Exchange said on Monday it has dropped Hanbo Steel Co Ltd from the 200 stocks making up the KOSPI-200 index, on which futures trading is based, because the stock was placed under the watch list.</p>
<p>Hanbo, which defaulted on debt repayments last Thursday, was replaced by Haitai Electronics Co, an exchange statement said.  </p>
<p>The KOSPI-200 index ended Monday's morning session down 1.24 points at 70.27 while the March futures contracts shed 1.6 points to 68.25.</p>
<p>Trading in Hanbo shares resumed on Monday after being suspended for the past two trading days. It ended the morning at 390 won lower at 4,570.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
